CAGE AT HOGWARTS

“Yer a wizard, Nicolas.”

“I’M A WHAT?”

It starts because Nicolas Cage gets a letter.

Not from Hogwarts.

From Costco.

At least that’s what he thinks.

He opens it.

Inside:

MR. NICOLAS CAGE
CUPBOARD UNDER THE STAIRS
SOMEWHERE HE SHOULD NOT BE

Cage stares.

Jessica: “That’s not our address.”

Cage: “Then they know too much.”

Little Nick climbs onto the envelope.

“Wax seal.”

Micro Nick squints at it.

“Hogwarts.”

Cage:

“Is that in Delaware?”

“No.”

“Good.”

Cut to Cage standing on Platform 9¾ wearing a trench coat over wizard robes and holding three suitcases, one containing only maps.

Jessica: “You don’t even know magic.”

Cage: “Neither does TSA, yet they remain powerful.”

Little Nick: “He’s got a point.”

Then the wall behind them explodes.

Not magically.

Just physically.

A black Dodge Charger somehow drives directly onto the platform.

The door opens.

Vin Diesel steps out.

No wand.

No robes.

Just a sleeveless shirt, boots, and the energy of a man who considers architecture optional.

He looks at Cage.

“Nicolas.”

Cage:

“Vin.”

They nod.

Jessica:

“You know each other?”

Vin:

“We’re family.”

Cage:

“I met him twice.”

Vin:

“Family doesn’t count meetings.”

Little Nick immediately whispers:

“He’s stronger than narrative.”

⸻

On the Hogwarts Express, everybody has wands.

Vin has a torque wrench.

Hermione asks:

“Is that enchanted?”

Vin:

“No.”

Ron:

“Then why bring it?”

Vin looks him dead in the eyes.

“Because bolts get loose.”

Silence.

Ron nods.

Fair.

Cage is meanwhile trying to buy something from the snack trolley using the Quarter.

Lady says:

“That’s American money.”

Cage:

“Currency is a social agreement.”

Lady:

“Two Sickles.”

Cage flips the Quarter.

It lands upright on the trolley.

The woman stares.

“…Fine.”

Little Nick:

“Exchange rate.”

⸻

They reach Hogwarts.

Sorting Hat goes on Cage.

Hat:

“Hmm…”

Cage:

“Take your time.”

Hat:

“You possess courage…”

Cage nods.

“Ambition…”

Nod.

“Loyalty…”

Nod.

“Intellectual curiosity…”

Bigger nod.

“…and absolutely catastrophic impulse control.”

Cage:

“Where does that put me?”

Sorting Hat:

“CUSTOMER SERVICE.”

Everyone goes silent.

McGonagall:

“That is not a house.”

Sorting Hat:

“It is now.”

Vin Diesel puts on the Hat.

It sits there for two seconds.

Hat:

“Family.”

Vin:

“Correct.”

Hat:

“…Gryffindor?”

Vin:

“Family.”

Hat sighs.

“Fine. Family.”

⸻

Then the doors open.

Professor Snape walks in.

Except Snape is Samuel L. Jackson.

Black robes.

Long black coat.

Absolutely furious for reasons no student fully understands.

He slams a book onto the desk.

“Turn to page three hundred and ninety-four.”

Cage raises hand.

Samuel L. Snape:

“What.”

Cage:

“Professor, respectfully, what happens on page three hundred and ninety-three?”

Snape slowly looks up.

“You wanna find out?”

Cage lowers hand.

“No, sir.”

Snape:

“That’s what I thought.”

He starts pacing.

“Today we are brewing Polyjuice Potion.”

Vin raises hand.

Snape:

“No.”

Vin:

“I didn’t ask yet.”

Snape:

“I know.”

Vin:

“What if instead of changing your appearance, you change your drivetrain?”

Snape stops.

Whole room still.

Snape:

“…what?”

Vin takes out a spark plug.

“Internal transformation.”

Snape stares at him for ten straight seconds.

Then:

“Ten points to whatever the hell you are.”

Vin:

“Family.”

Snape:

“Minus five.”

⸻

Cage is absolutely terrible at potions.

Not because he lacks talent.

Because he refuses to follow measurements.

Hermione:

“It says precisely three drops.”

Cage:

“Three is conservative.”

He pours half the bottle.

Little Nick:

“Boss.”

Cage:

“We need potency.”

Micro Nick crawls out of his sleeve.

“Volatile.”

Cage:

“Good.”

The cauldron starts whispering.

Nobody notices at first.

Then it says:

“Nicolas.”

Cage freezes.

Jessica, from across the room:

“No.”

Cage leans closer.

“Nicolas…”

Snape:

“Mr. Cage, back away from the cauldron.”

Cage:

“It knows my name.”

Snape:

“YOU LABELLED IT.”

Sure enough, masking tape on side:

NICOLAS’S POTION — DO NOT TOUCH

Cage:

“…could be unrelated.”

Then the cauldron grows Nicolas Cage’s face.

Snape:

“Motherf—”

BOOM.

Purple smoke everywhere.

When it clears, every student in the room looks like Nicolas Cage.

Harry Cage.

Ron Cage.

Hermione Cage.

Draco Cage.

Even Snape Cage.

Samuel L. Jackson looks down at himself.

Now he has Nicolas Cage’s face but still Samuel L. Jackson’s voice.

Long silence.

Then:

“WHICH ONE OF YOU MOTHERFUCKERS DID THIS?”

Every Nicolas Cage in the room points at original Nicolas Cage.

Cage points at Vin.

Vin:

“Family doesn’t snitch.”

Snape:

“I AM ABOUT TO EXPEL AN ENTIRE BLOODLINE.”

⸻

But here’s the problem.

The potion doesn’t stop at appearances.

Everybody starts gradually becoming more Nicolas Cage.

Draco Cage grabs a candlestick.

“THIS CASTLE IS LYING TO US.”

Hermione Cage starts drawing red string between portraits.

Ron Cage is yelling at a staircase:

“YOU CAN’T JUST MOVE WHENEVER YOU WANT. THAT’S ANARCHY.”

Harry Cage looks into the Mirror of Erised.

He sees Nicolas Cage.

He turns around.

“WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?”

Cage:

“Don’t ask questions you aren’t emotionally prepared to answer.”

Vin is completely unaffected.

Jessica:

“Why didn’t it work on you?”

Vin:

“I already know who I am.”

Little Nick whispers:

“Jesus.”

⸻

Dumbledore convenes an emergency meeting.

Except before he can speak, the doors slam open.

Big Nick ducks into the Great Hall.

He is wearing Hagrid’s coat like a vest.

Dumbledore:

“Who is this?”

Cage:

“Management.”

Big Nick:

“THERE’S A PROBLEM IN THE DUNGEON.”

Snape Cage:

“There are always problems in the dungeon.”

Big Nick:

“THIS ONE HAS A NOSFERATU FACE AND NO NOSE.”

Everybody goes quiet.

Voldemort walks in.

Also Nicolas Cage.

Nobody had dosed him.

He just looks like Cage already.

Jessica:

“…Okay, now that’s concerning.”

Voldemort Cage:

“At last, Nicolas.”

Cage:

“Have we met?”

Voldemort:

“In another continuity.”

Micro Nick immediately faints.

Little Nick:

“Oh, that’s bad.”

⸻

Voldemort raises wand.

“Avada—”

Vin Diesel steps between them.

“No.”

Voldemort:

“What?”

Vin:

“You don’t kill family.”

Voldemort:

“We are not family.”

Vin:

“We’re standing in the same room.”

Voldemort:

“That is not how family works.”

Vin takes one step closer.

“It is now.”

Even Voldemort hesitates.

Snape Cage whispers:

“I have no fucking idea whose class this is anymore.”

⸻

Cage suddenly notices something.

The Elder Wand.

The Quarter.

The Sorting Hat.

Three artifacts.

Three decision systems.

He whispers:

“Third option.”

Jessica:

“Oh no.”

Cage throws the Quarter into the Sorting Hat.

Vin throws in the torque wrench.

Snape, for reasons known only to Samuel L. Jackson, throws in a flask labeled:

DO NOT FUCKING DRINK

The Hat begins shaking.

“WHAT ARE YOU DOING?”

Cage:

“Cross-platform compatibility.”

Hat:

“THAT DOESN’T MEAN ANYTHING.”

Lightning.

The Hat fires a beam into the Elder Wand.

Every staircase in Hogwarts reconfigures at once.

The castle becomes a giant parking garage.

Vin looks around.

Slowly smiles.

“Now this makes sense.”

Cage:

“Vin?”

Vin walks toward a broomstick.

“No.”

He grabs a Thestral carriage.

“Too slow.”

Then he sees the Hogwarts Express.

He looks at Cage.

Cage looks at Vin.

Jessica:

“No.”

Vin:

“Family.”

Cage:

“Jurisdiction.”

Samuel L. Snape:

“Absolutely the fuck not.”

Cut to:

THE HOGWARTS EXPRESS DRIFTING AROUND THE ASTRONOMY TOWER.

Vin is driving.

Cage is hanging out the side with a wand.

Little Nick is on the roof yelling directions.

Micro Nick is somehow conducting the train.

Snape is chasing them on a broom screaming:

“GET BACK HERE, YOU BALD-HEADED AUTOMOTIVE SON OF A—”

Vin:

“Need more steam.”

Cage:

“We’re at maximum steam.”

Vin:

“There’s always more.”

He reaches down and shifts a lever that should not exist.

The train accelerates.

Dumbledore watches from a window.

McGonagall:

“Should we stop them?”

Dumbledore:

“No.”

“Why?”

He takes a sip of tea.

“Because I would very much like to see where this goes.”

And deep beneath Hogwarts, the Marauder’s Map updates.

Not with footsteps.

With one new label moving at 140 miles per hour:

NICOLAS CAGE, VIN DIESEL, AND SEVERAL ACTIVE FELONIES

Fade to black.

